menu "C5VRX board"

    choice C5VRX_BOARD
        prompt "Board and video output"
        default C5VRX_BOARD_XIAO_DAC
        help
            Where the received video goes. The XIAO build recovers the
            composite waveform onto the six-bit resistor DAC. The Waveshare
            build shows the picture and the menu on the board's 1.47"
            ST7789 LCD, and the DAC's 5 (or 6, USB off) upper bits on
            header pins (docs/LCD147.md).

        config C5VRX_BOARD_XIAO_DAC
            bool "XIAO ESP32-C5 with the resistor DAC (composite out)"

        config C5VRX_BOARD_WAVESHARE_LCD147
            bool "Waveshare ESP32-C5-LCD-1.47 (picture on the LCD)"
    endchoice

    config C5VRX_LCD_SPI_MHZ
        int "LCD SPI clock (MHz)"
        depends on C5VRX_BOARD_WAVESHARE_LCD147
        range 10 80
        default 40
        help
            40 MHz is Waveshare's example clock. The ST7789 is specified to
            62.5 MHz writes; 80 MHz is outside the datasheet.

    config C5VRX_LCD_FLIP
        bool "Turn the LCD picture by 180 degrees"
        depends on C5VRX_BOARD_WAVESHARE_LCD147
        default n
        help
            Off: Waveshare's landscape orientation (their examples'
            rotation 3).

endmenu
